Blackdrift: replace the Focus wordmark, onboarding logo and splash mark.

Why: wordmark2 ("Firefox Focus", home screen, About, biometric lock),
onboarding_logo (first onboarding screen) and ic_splash_screen (splash and
search widget icon) are Mozilla marks. Same-name vectors in src/focus/res
replace them, so no layout or Kotlin call site changes. wordmark2 is the
Clean Slate lockup (mark plus lowercase "blackdrift" in Albert Sans Light, as
outlines, so no font is bundled), 296dp wide so the ten-letter word keeps the
old lockup's letter size; onboarding_logo, drawn in a fixed 150dp square, is
the stacked lockup (mark above the word); the splash is the mark on the launcher's
108dp grid. They are coloured through the blackdrift_* brand tokens added here
(values-night swaps them), so they stay readable on light and dark themes.
The splash background colour is set in Focus's colors.xml by 0208. Verbatim
copies of blackdrift/branding/android/focus/res, generated by build.mjs.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

